Paperlike Control is an independent, unofficial macOS client for DASUNG
Paperlike 13K monitors.

It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by DASUNG / 大上科技.

Protocol notes
--------------
The USB-serial framing used here (24-character uppercase ASCII hex packets
starting with 5FF5 and ending with A0FA, CH340 1a86:7523 at 115200 8N1) was
documented by community reverse engineering, including:

- https://github.com/roflecopter/paperlike13k_linux
- https://github.com/plateaukao/paperlike13k_macos
- https://github.com/codefastdieyoung/paperlike-rs

Those projects did not publish a license at the time this repository was
created. This tree does not copy their source files. Command IDs and packet
layout are interoperability facts about the hardware.

The Unix socket at $TMPDIR/paperlike.sock accepts the same JSON request shape
as plateaukao's Python CLI so existing `paperlike --refresh` wrappers keep
working. That compatibility is reimplemented here, not vendored.

Stillcolor-style GPU dithering uses public IOMobileFramebuffer properties
also used by DASUNG's Mac client (`enableDither`, `uniformity2D`).
